From 48fdfb08a797707539c0f81ea20e395e97ec397e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Patch <patch@example.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 01:29:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hr): audit trail, leave balances, employee search,
 idempotent payroll

Several HR features were either stubbed out or silently no-ops:

- AuditLog was never written to anywhere. hr/audit_logs.html always
  rendered an empty table, and the HR dashboard's "Recent Changes" card
  was two hardcoded fake entries that never changed. Added
  _log_hr_action() and wired it into every mutating HR route (employee
  create/update/deactivate/delete, rota generation, allowance/deduction
  creation, leave request/approve/reject, payroll generation); index()
  and audit_logs() now read real rows.

- hr/index.html's "Active Employees" / "Inactive Employees" dashboard
  cards linked to employee_list?status=active/inactive, but the route
  ignored request.args entirely and always returned every employee.
  employee_list() now honors status, department, and a new free-text
  search (name or employee ID), with a filter bar in the template.

- Leave requests had no date validation, no overlap detection, and no
  entitlement tracking at all: an employee could submit end_date before
  start_date, double-book overlapping leave, or take unlimited vacation.
  Added Employee.annual_leave_days (default 21, Kenya Employment Act
  minimum), Employee.leave_days_used()/leave_days_remaining(), a
  Leave.days property, a WTForms date-order validator, and overlap +
  balance checks in leave_request(). Balance is surfaced on the leave
  request form and the employee profile.

- generate_payroll() had no idempotency: re-running it for a month
  already generated inserted duplicate Payroll rows per employee instead
  of recalculating, silently doubling reported pay. It now
  updates the existing record for that employee/month if one exists.

Includes an Alembic migration for the new employees.annual_leave_days
column and 22 new regression tests in tests/test_hr_module.py (56 passed
total, 978 tests still collect cleanly across the suite).
